    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter: reference Npcs.json Id 4099 drawn at [-1545.52, -57.75, 1215.97] (npc_spawns_extra.json spawn_guid 100000004099, FreeRealms-Legacy FabledRealms.lua). Region The Wilds, place The Wilds."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 44 ('Explosive Robgoblins! (the live random encounter: robgoblin boomers tossing dynamite)'): scene sg_random_encounter_skullcamp, entry, exit, 4 waves, 19 spawns ({'Robgoblin Boomer': 16, 'Robgoblin Bruiser': 2, 'Robgoblin Kaboomer': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1241 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_skullcamp has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 75 coins / 260 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "capture",
      "evidence": "rc-0136 (2026-11-11): model 1682 robgoblin_m_master.adr, the model live sent for every Robgoblin Kaboomer (10 AddNpc rows in packets_3.pcapng, 2014-03); 4202 robgoblin_m_junkmaster.adr was the reference row's."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 prize wheel (2026-11-12): 'Explosive Robgoblins!' has no wheel of its own on the wiki; the wiki's item pages put its prize wheel with 'Bergram Stumpfinger' (Ninja's Shadow Blade of Deception; Wizard's Ornate Wand of Transmutation; Warrior’s Warlord Axe of Thunder; Medic's Shockrod of Lasers), so it spins that wheel, from our record dungeons/bergram_stumpfinger_s_ghost.json, one per combat job, and 26 coins. The same pages also name Bergram Stumpfinger's Ghost. Archer from our record dungeons/bergram_stumpfinger_s_ghost.json; Brawler from our record dungeons/bergram_stumpfinger_s_ghost.json; Medic from our record dungeons/bergram_stumpfinger_s_ghost.json; Medic: 'Energy Transfer Medic Pants' is in no catalogue or record, left off; Ninja from our record dungeons/bergram_stumpfinger_s_ghost.json; Warrior from our record dungeons/bergram_stumpfinger_s_ghost.json; Wizard from our record dungeons/bergram_stumpfinger_s_ghost.json."
